    "chunk_size_bytes": 2006,
    "chunk_text": "Eleventh Paragraph:It is ordained that the reproductions of the Decoration in miniature, which may be worn oncertain occasions by those upon whom the Decoration is conferred, shall be half the size of theKariyakshama Seva Vibhushanaya.\n\nTwelfth Paragraph:It is ordained that sealed patterns of the Kariyakshama Seva Vibhushana, and its miniatures, areheld by the appropriate authority at the Sri Lanka Army Headquarters.\n\nFourteenth Paragraph :It is ordained that the Decoration shall be conferred under such regulation as to grant forfeiture,restoration, and other matters in amplification of this my Proclamation as may with my approvalsignified through the Secretary Defence be issued from time to time by the Commander of theSri Lanka Army.\n\nFifteenth Paragraph:I reserve to myself and my elected Successors the full power of annulling, abrogating,augmenting, interpreting or dispensing with these rules and regulations, or any part thereof bya Notification under my Seal and Signature, or under my Command.\n\nBy His Excellency\u2019s Command,\n\nUDAYA R. SENEVIRATNE,Secretary to the President.\n\nOffice of Secretary to the President,Colombo,11th November, 2019.\n\n12 - 114/1\n\n3AI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'11'21PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA - 21.11.2019\n\nAMENDMENT\n\nKARIYAKSHAMA SEVA PADAKKAMA\n\nOrders\n\nREGULATIONS mentioned in the following paragraphs, numbered as Fourthly, Fifthly, Sixthly, Seventhly, Eighthly, Ninthly,Tenthly, Eleventhly, Twelfthly and Thirteenthly published in the Government Gazette Extraordinary Number 412/20dated 01.08.1986, of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka pertaining to Kariyakshama Seva Padakkama arehereby amended.\n\nWhereas I am desirous of rewarding long, efficient loyal service, and exemplary conduct of proven capacity byCommissioned Officers, Warrant Officers, Non-Commissioned Officers and Men of the Sri Lanka Army Volunteer Force."
