    "chunk_text": "2. Here by declare that trading in the temple premises is prohibited. The conducting of trading activities and dansalcould be done along the main road and the by-roads upto the Sri Pada Vihara but without any obstruction to thedevotees and the Pageant.\n\n3. Hereby declare that collection of aids and contributions are prohibited from Pelmadulla Town up to Sri PadaTemple premises.\n\n5. The Ceylon Electricity Board and the Pradeshiya Sabhawa of Pelmadulla are entrusted with the work of fixingstreet lamps and extra lamps in the temple premises and its surroundings roads.\n\n6. Prior to and after the pegeant festival matters related to health care and sanitary and removal of garbage areentrusted with the Pelmadulla Pradeshiya Sabhawa and office of the medical officer of health.\n\n7. The branch office of the Water Supplies and Drainage Board is entrusted with the work of provision of water bykeeping extra water tanks.\n\n8. The police and security services are entrusted with all sort of security measures on the traffic controlling requiredfor uninterrupted conduct of the pageant and moments of devottees.\n\n9. The statute and the relics will be worshipped and offerings will be given at the Sri Pada Station for six months andafter the day of coming Wesak Poya day those will be deposited at Deity's Palace at Raja Maha Vihara ofGalpoththawala and worshipped and offerings will be given. The above 8 orders are valid until to that day.\n\nB. S. G. RUWANSIRI,Divisional Secretary,Pelmadulla.\n\n12 - 435\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
