    "chunk_text": "wxl 2152$3 - 2019 foie\u00efn\u00be ui 02 jeks i`\u00ffod - 2019'12'02\n\nNo. 2152/3 \u2013 MONDAY, DECEMBER 02, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nG 31602 - 17 (2019/12)\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nNotice under Section 7\n\nMy No.: DHO/LAN/ACQTN/A3/2/11.\n\nLands and Parliamentary Reforms Ministry's\n\nReference No.: 4-3/8/2016/mS\u00e3$451.\n\nI hereby give notice, under Sub-section (1) of Section 7 ofthe Land Acquisition (Amendment) Act, No.28 of 1964, thatthe Government intends to acquire the following land/servitude which is required for a public purpose:\n\nDescription of the Land to be Acquired:\n\nAllotment of lands described below and depicted inPreliminary Plan No. 3697 dated 29.07.2019 situated in the Villageof Atulugama in Grama Niladhari Division of No. 116 CKanangama in Divisional Secretary's Division of Dehiowita inKegalle District in Sabaragamuwa Province.\n\n1. Lot No. 01Name of the Land: Dewalakanda Estates - Part ofAkkaramalaya; Land Use: Watta, Rubber Plantation of\n\n15- 20 years, present ownership; Claimants: KelaniweliPlantations PLC, No. 400, Deans Road, Colombo 10; Extent:0.8094 hec.\n\nAll persons interested, in the aforesaid land servitude arehereby required to appear personally, or by agents dulyauthorized in writing, before me at Divisional SecretariatDehiowita, on16th January 2020 at 10.00 a.m. further, it shouldbe notifed in writing (in duplicate) on or before 03rd January2020 regarding the nature of their interests in the land theparticulars of their claims for compensation for the acquisitionof the said lands, the amount of compensation and the detailsof the computation of such amount.\n\nU. P. CHANDANA ANURUDDHA PIYADASA,\n\nDivisional Secretary,\n\nDehiowita.\n\nAt the Divisional Secretariat,Dehiowita,22nd November, 2019.\n\n12- 524"
  },
