    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'12'03Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 03.12.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2152$9 - 2019 foie\u00efn\u00be ui 03 jeks w\u00d5yrejdod - 2019'12'03No. 2152/9 - TUESDAY DECEMBER 03, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF MEMBER OF THE VAVUNIYA (TAMIL) SOUTHPRADESHIYA SABHA UNDER SECTION 66A(1) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIES ELECTIONSORDINANCE (CHAPTER 262)\n\nWHEREAS the office of return member of Vavuniya (Tamil) South Pradeshiya Sabha has fallen vacant by reason ofResignation ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the Eelam People\u2019s Democratic Party, the recognized political party to whichSelvarasa Reegan the member belonged, was required by me under Section 66 A (1) of the aforesaid ordinance, to decideupon returned member of Eelam People\u2019s Democratic Party who belongs to such party and is not disqualified underSection 9 of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance and who shall be declared selected as a member within a periodof thirty (30) days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the aforesaid recognized Political Party has communicated his decision tonominate Tharmakunasingam Sujivan to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, Malawenna Godage Lalith Ananda, Returning Officer of the Vavuniya (Tamil) SouthPradeshiya Sabha, acting in terms of Section 66A(1) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) dohereby declare that Tharmakunasingam Sujivan was selected as the member of the Vavuniya (Tamil) South PradeshiyaSabha.\n\nM. G. LALITH ANANDA,Returning Officer,Vavuniya (Tamil) South Pradeshiya Sabha.District Election Office,Vavuniya,02nd December, 2019.\n\n12 - 557/1\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT\n\nNotices under the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance"
